+/* ══ 7 · `-1lh` SURVIVES THE BUILD — A LABELLED GUARD, NOT A GATE ══════════════════════════ */
+
+test("GUARD (not a gate): the built stylesheet still carries `-1lh`", async () => {
+  // THIS CANNOT FAIL FROM THE TOOLCHAIN and it says so in its own name. Lightning CSS passes a
+  // unit through at every target, so `calc(-1lh - …)` is emitted verbatim whatever the floor
+  // is; the only thing this catches is a human deleting the pull. The row that CAN fail — the
+  // browserslist floor sitting UNDER the unit, which drops the whole margin shorthand at
+  // computed-value time on a real client — is check 6 of `scripts/check-support-floor.mjs`,
+  // where it is re-derived against the declaration rather than grepped out of an artifact.
